# Expectation record for 02_constant_expressions/003_static_assert.c
#
# Reproduce one cell by hand with no harness: render the three command templates
# below, substituting the target triple, the optimization level, the source path,
# the output path, and the target's runner (empty on the natively executing target).

program            = 003_static_assert
area               = 02_constant_expressions
description        = _Static_assert on satisfied conditions across the type system, folded and volatile-runtime
targets            = x86_64, i686, aarch64, riscv64
opt_levels         = -O0, -O1, -O2
shared_flags       = -static
bcc_command        = $BCC --target <triple> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
ref_command        = $REF_CC_<TRIPLE> <opt> -static <src> -o <out>
run_command        = <runner> <out>
expect_exit        = 0
oracle_a           = enabled
oracle_b           = enabled
oracle_c           = enabled
ub_notes           <<END
This program contains no undefined and no unspecified behaviour, which is the property
both differential oracles rest on: undefined behaviour would license either compiler to do
anything and would make a divergence prove nothing about either.
Every _Static_assert in the file is SATISFIED, and that is a soundness requirement rather
than a preference. Both mandated oracles compare the observable behaviour of a binary that
was built successfully, so a deliberately failing assertion would stop compilation under
both compilers and leave nothing to compare; error detection -- the correct rejection of an
invalid program -- is a noted non-goal of this suite for exactly that reason.
No arithmetic can overflow. The folded expressions are the small constants 2 + 3 * 4,
(1 << 10) >> 4 and 4294967296LL / 65536, and each runtime twin recomputes precisely that
value from volatile operands of the same types, so no intermediate leaves the range of int
or long long. Both shift counts, 10 and 4, are within the range of the 32-bit promoted left
operand. Both divisions have a non-zero divisor: 65536 is a literal, and the one division
by a measured value is guarded by a positivity test on both operands, so a divisor of zero
cannot reach it even if a measurement were to fail.
No storage is read uninitialized. The ten probe arrays have static storage duration and are
therefore zero-initialized, and their contents are never read at all -- only the byte
distance between two of their element addresses is taken. Every automatic object is
initialized in its own declaration, including the volatile pair array in the local-type
probe, whose members are read back afterwards.
Pointer arithmetic stays in range. Both operands of every subtraction address bytes of one
and the same object, so each difference is defined. The single one-past-end pointer,
table + TABLE_LEN, is formed and subtracted but never dereferenced. The bounded string scan
stops at the array's own size, so it cannot read past the terminator whatever the array
holds. Every reinterpretation of an object's bytes is through a character type, so no
aliasing rule is broken, and nothing depends on padding bytes or on the relative addresses
of unrelated objects.
No object is modified twice between sequence points, no call receives more than one argument
with a side effect, and the program reads no clock, no environment, no file and no socket:
every input is a literal in the source.
No header is included and printf is declared by hand, so nothing here depends on a standard
library header bcc does not ship. _Static_assert and _Alignof are C11 keywords and need no
header; stdalign.h is deliberately not included, because it would only add the lowercase
alignas and alignof macro spellings. Every assertion uses the two-argument form with a
message, because the message-less form is C23 and the default gate's -pedantic -Werror
rejects it.
This record declares no warning-gate deviation: the program is clean under the full default
gate -Wall -Wextra -pedantic -Wconversion -Wsign-conversion -Wshadow -Werror at every
optimization level with all four reference drivers, and clean under the sanitizer gate.
END
impl_defined_notes <<END
This record narrows nothing -- all four targets, all three optimization levels and all three
oracles are enabled -- and these notes exist to record how that was achieved, because the
type system is exactly where a program of this kind would otherwise have had to narrow.
Every _Static_assert is true on all four targets, which is the condition that makes the
four-way comparison possible at all: an assertion that failed on one target would break the
build there rather than report a divergence. Two kinds of condition are used to guarantee
that. Exact values are asserted only for the quantities measured to be identical on all four
targets: sizeof char, short, int, long long, float and double are 1, 2, 4, 8, 4 and 8, and
_Alignof char, short, int and float are 1, 2, 4 and 4. Everything else is asserted as a
RELATION, which holds whatever the individual values are.
The target-varying properties are therefore covered without being pinned. Pointer width and
sizeof(long) are 4 bytes on i686 and 8 on x86-64, AArch64 and RISC-V 64, so this program
asserts and prints only that long is exactly pointer width, that size_t is exactly pointer
width, and that ptrdiff_t is exactly pointer width -- each true on all four. sizeof(long
double) was measured at 16, 12, 16 and 16 bytes across x86-64, i686, AArch64 and RISC-V 64
(x87 80-bit versus IEEE binary128), so it appears only inside the ordering relation
sizeof(double) <= sizeof(long double), and its size is never printed. The alignments of
double and long long likewise appear only in relations. size_t and ptrdiff_t are probed
without being named -- as sizeof(sizeof(int)) and as sizeof of a pointer difference --
because naming them would require stddef.h, and this program includes no header.
Plain char signedness was measured as signed on x86-64 and i686 and unsigned on AArch64 and
RISC-V 64, so it is never asserted and never observed. Plain char appears only as a
one-byte size probe whose signedness cannot affect a size, and the one character value that
is printed is read from an explicitly signed char holding 65, which every char signedness
represents exactly.
THE EXECUTION CHARACTER SET IS A SEPARATE IMPLEMENTATION-DEFINED PROPERTY FROM CHAR
SIGNEDNESS, AND IT IS PINNED RATHER THAN ASSUMED. Routing a character through an explicitly
signed char settles the signedness question and settles nothing about which code the letter
carries: C11 5.2.1 leaves the members of the execution character set and their codes
implementation-defined, so an implementation is free to place A somewhere other than 65.
Exactly two printed lines observe a character's value here -- fold_char_a, which prints
(int)'A' from a constant expression, and run_char_a, which prints the same value back out of
the signed char -- and nothing else in the program observes one: msg is measured only by its
size and by the offset of its terminator, probe_char only by its element size, and no line
renders a literal. A single assertion therefore closes the whole accounting, and the program
carries it: _Static_assert('A' == 65, "the execution character set places A at 65 (ASCII) on
this target"). All four enabled targets were measured to use the same ASCII-family basic
execution character set, so the condition holds on every cell of this record's matrix. The
assertion is the mechanism that keeps the two oracles honest: on an implementation whose
character set differed, the cell would FAIL TO TRANSLATE naming the reason -- accusing the
environment, where the difference actually lives -- instead of printing a different number
that oracle (a) or oracle (b) would charge to the compiler under test. A future target that
disagreed would announce itself at the build, and the correct response would be to narrow
this record's target list with the reason recorded here, never to delete the assertion or the
two lines it protects.
Two implementation-defined layout facts are relied on and were verified rather than assumed.
struct triple is int, short, unsigned char and union scalar_bytes has an 8-byte widest
member; the standard leaves their exact sizes to the implementation, and both were measured
at 8 bytes on all four targets, which is what licenses printing those two sizes raw. The
shapes were chosen for that reason: an aggregate whose padding depended on the alignment of
double or long long would have sized differently on i686, where those alignments are 4
rather than 8. If a target ever laid these out differently while remaining conforming, the
resulting difference would be an implementation-defined divergence rather than a compiler
defect, and it would have to be recorded as an expected divergence with this record's target
list narrowed and the reason stated here -- never left to surface as a finding against a
backend that did nothing wrong, and never resolved by deleting the aggregate assertions,
which would remove coverage this program exists to provide. The size of the enumerated type
is implementation-defined too, and it is deliberately neither asserted nor printed; only the
enumerator values, which their constant expressions fix, are.
The exact per-target alignments and widths that this program declines to pin are not left
untested elsewhere: 10_declarations_and_types/007_alignof_alignas.c pins them exactly,
selecting the expectation from the architecture predefined macro. The division of labour is
deliberate, so that neither program needs a restricted target list.
END
expected_stdout    <<END
static_assert_count=34
static_assert_contexts=5
fold_sizes=1 2 4 8 4 8
run_strides=1 2 4 8 4 8
fold_size_order=1 1
run_size_order=1 1
fold_long_is_ptr_width=1
run_long_is_ptr_width=1
fold_width_probes=1 1
run_width_probes=1 1
fold_alignments=1 2 4 4
run_alignments=1 2 4 4
fold_align_bounds=1 1
run_align_bounds=1 1
fold_arith=14 64
run_arith=14 64
fold_wide_arith=65536
run_wide_arith=65536
fold_char_a=65
run_char_a=65
fold_enumerators=0 2 10 -1
run_enumerators=0 2 10 -1
fold_table_len=7
run_table_len=7
fold_string_sizes=4 4 1
run_string_size=4
fold_aggregate_sizes=8 8
run_aggregate_strides=8 8
fold_aggregate_bounds=1 1 1
run_aggregate_bounds=1 1 1
fold_local_type=1 1 110
run_local_type=1 1 110
END
